    {
     "head": "Glucose",
     "group": "glucose",
     "text": "Glucose comes from digested food. It is absorbed in the small intestine and is carried, dissolved in the _plasma_, to every cell. It then diffuses into the cells."
    },
    {
     "head": "Oxygen",
     "group": "oxygen",
     "text": "Oxygen comes from the air in the lungs. It diffuses from the alveoli into the blood, and it is carried by _haemoglobin_ in the red blood cells. Oxygen then diffuses from the capillaries into the cells."
    },
    {
     "head": "Carbon dioxide",
     "group": "co2",
     "text": "Carbon dioxide diffuses from the cells into the blood. It is carried in the plasma to the lungs, where it diffuses into the alveoli and is breathed out."
    },
    {
     "head": "Water",
     "group": "water",
     "text": "Water stays in the body, or it is lost in urine, in sweat and in expired air (the air that is breathed out)."
    }
